WEBVTT

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.860
Nice shot, Aoyama!

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.420
A-o-ya-ma-kun!

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:07.490
Sakai!

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.740
Good luck, Sakai-senpai!

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.460
You're amazing! Yay!

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.650
Sakai-senpai!

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.780
He's blushing! How cute!

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.790
Why are they getting all 
worked up over Sakai?

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.370
They don't even do that for me,
and I'm freakin' hot!

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:31.840
Dude, you're actually in our league.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:34.920
I wonder why he's so popular 
all of a sudden.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.540
Come to think of it,
he's changed his hairstyle.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:14.610
<b>#11</b>

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.610
<b>Sakai-kun's Hairstyle Has Changed</b>

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.700
Heya.

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:18.130
Huh? Sakai isn't here.

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:19.840
Hey, Aoyama, have you seen Saka—

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:20.780
It's me.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.290
Stop trying to look cool!

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:35.460
What's with that hair? You look like Aoyama!

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.150
Is this a wig? Is it?

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:45.290
I've always had hair like this.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:48.130
I'm gonna go on ahead.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:56.190
<b>I ♥
Sakai</b>

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.580
Aren't there more of them now?

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.190
Looks like it.

00:02:56.990 --> 00:03:00.950
Is he trying to get on
the "handsome team"?

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:00.950
Sakai-kun!

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.810
Good luck, Sakai-kun!

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:07.950
Oh, my God!

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.340
We won't tolerate defectors!

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:12.580
Triple sliding tackle!

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.990
So cool!

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.290
Huh?

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:22.300
Are you trying to be mops?

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:23.090
<b>Mop Team</b>

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:25.970
Thanks for cleaning the field.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:38.850
Sakai-kun, you're so cool! 
Please go out with me!

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:44.930
U-Um, Senpai...

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:45.550
Huh?

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.620
What?!

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.870
I-I baked these in class. 
If you want them...

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.300
Thanks.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.180
How dare you?!

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:06.330
You guys want some?

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:07.810
Ha, you wish!

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:09.070
We're going to eat them all!

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:11.020
Sakai-senpai!

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:12.900
Please have these!

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.700
Please eat mine, too!

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.420
Thanks!

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.970
Sakai's looking good lately.

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:21.930
You said it, girl.

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:30.680
Sakai's changed, huh?

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:33.860
No, he couldn't have changed that quickly!

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.080
Right?

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.840
We're going to unearth the real Sakai!

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.390
Sa-ka-i! Sa-ka-i!

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:43.990
Sa-ka-i! Sa-ka-i!

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:56.470
Sakai! Come on, Sakai!

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:58.580
There it is!

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:01.110
Fujimi's specialty: butt keepie-uppie!

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.490
<i>What do you say now, Sakai?!
We're serving up your favorite: butt jokes!</i>

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.820
<i>Surely you can't resist the urge!</i>

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:15.020
You're so silly.

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:22.640
So smooth!

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:23.880
Sakai...

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:28.700
Come back, Sakai! Come home, Sakai!

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.970
Why? How did this happen?!

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.450
Oh, Sakai-senpai!

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:34.580
Um...

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:40.470
I-I'm in love with you.

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:42.590
I'm serious! Please go out with me.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:43.440
No, with me!

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.890
Huh?!

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:46.090
What's your deal?

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:47.450
Hey!

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:55.200
I'm sad to say that Sakai's 
gone over to the other side.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:57.660
Let's at least see him off.

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:00.290
Since when do you like him?

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:00.960
I'm sorry.

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:03.080
I can't.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:03.960
What?!

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.420
What's this?

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:08.260
I... I...

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:11.970
Sakai!

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:14.600
I can't belong to just one person.

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:22.430
I'm everyone's Sakai!

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:25.610
So cool!

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:31.490
Oh, really now.

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:39.750
Sakai's 
Poetry 
Reading

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:36.130
"The world is beautiful."

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:39.750
"Why, you ask?"

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:42.920
<b>Poetry by Moi</b>

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:42.420
"Because I exist."

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:46.510
<b>Poetry by Moi</b>

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:46.500
"Now, come into the Sakai fold."

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:53.040
He really is in a faraway place now.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:54.140
Yeah.

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:55.910
Sakai...

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.530
Sakai scored again!

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:15.160
Sa-ka-i! Sa-ka-i! Sa-ka-i!

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:06.930
Impressive.

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:09.900
But what about all that nonsense?

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.910
If our team gets stronger 
for it, I welcome it.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.160
Zaizen!

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:19.790
If one of our defenders can score, 
it definitely helps the team.

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:21.840
But you know...

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:23.040
Right?

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:26.670
Sakai. Don't worry about those guys.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:30.170
You just keep on scoring goals,
 left, right, and center!

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:31.430
Let's storm the Nationals together!

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:35.250
Zaizen, you should know this about me.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:38.990
I don't give a damn about Nationals.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:42.660
All I want to do is score!

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:43.690
Huh?

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:45.770
So switch positions with me!

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.740
From now on, I'll be a forward!

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:48.570
What?!

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.950
That sounds like a good idea,
 Sakai playing up front.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.570
Coach!

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:57.250
I can hear the voice of the God of Soccer.

00:07:57.250 --> 00:08:00.220
Score goals! Go! Go! Go!

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:04.180
He's whispering to me, 
telling me to score goals!

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:04.180
Score goals! Go!

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:06.340
<i>I'm actually starting to get pissed now!</i>

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:09.960
<i>I've been a forward my entire life.</i>

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:18.470
Sakai again!

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.180
He's unstoppable!

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:28.420
Sa-ka-i! Sa-ka-i! Sa-ka-i!

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:26.290
I can hear it. I can hear it!

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:29.170
Thanks for missing the ball for me.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:35.350
The desire to be attractive and stand out
has turned Sakai into a goal poacher.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:39.690
Sakai's actually amazing.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:42.120
He looks every inch a striker.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.470
And...

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:46.750
This Sakai might actually 
be funny in his own way!

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:51.730
Converting Sakai into a forward 
might not be a bad move.

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:52.690
What?

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:57.540
<i>At this rate, I really 
might lose my position.</i>

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:58.460
Sakai of the world! Sakai of the world!

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:00.010
Beautiful!

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:01.310
This is when I need...

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:03.270
...Aoyama!

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:06.230
There it is!

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:07.980
I need to score!

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:12.230
Go! Go! Go!

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:13.990
Sakai!

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:16.740
Aoyama!

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:18.410
Thanks!

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:20.300
Sakai!

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:23.280
Nice shot, Sakai-san.

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:25.370
<i>What? Even Aoyama?!</i>

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:27.040
Sakai!

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.880
He's the real deal!

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:32.350
<i>At this rate... At this rate...</i>

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:36.380
<b>[Super Effective Boy]</b>

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:36.380
<b>A cleaning hero 
born in Germany</b>

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:36.380
Eliminates stains with just water

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:36.380
Fujimi High School scores!

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:40.870
We made it to Nationals!

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:43.390
Hooray, hooray.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.210
Hooray, hooray.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:46.130
Hooray, hooray, amazing.

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:48.740
Hooray, hooray.

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.400
<i>I </i>cannot<i> do this!</i>

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.300
Sa-ka-i! Sa-ka-i!

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:53.170
Amazing Sakai!

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:54.650
Go!

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:57.400
I heard it, too.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:59.940
That whisper you were talking about.

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:06.790
What's wrong with you, Zaizen?
Don't mark your own teammate!

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:10.590
When he gets a sniff of a chance, I'm going 
to steal the ball from under his nose!

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:12.910
I heard that.

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:16.920
A smart pass from Aoyama!

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.680
What are they doing?!

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:24.680
<i>Even if people decry me as acting dirty,</i>

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:28.200
<i>my dream is to take Fujimi 
High School to the Nationals!</i>

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.730
<i>And it goes without saying...</i>

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:32.690
<i>...with me on the field!</i>

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.710
Goal!

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:41.070
Fujimi High School scores a fifth goal!

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:43.070
Sa-ka-i of the world!

00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:48.080
D-D-D-Dash! Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:50.970
That number 3's amazing, too.

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:53.340
I didn't know Fujimi had a forward like him.

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:57.570
Oh, speaking of which, where's that big guy?

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:58.800
<b>Fujimi</b>

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:58.800
<b>Kanehira</b>

00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:00.220
More importantly, over here!

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:02.830
Now that we have a buffer...

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:05.740
Kaocchi, I think you can 
start warming up now.

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:07.260
Sure.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:12.020
<b>I know that I'm the
 one true hot guy</b>

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:12.020
<b>Tada Hikaru</b>

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:15.020
<b>[Spot the 5 Differences]</b>

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:15.020
<b>A quiet fool</b>

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:15.020
<b>Satou Kiyoshi</b>

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:20.980
Kaoru, I heard that you weren't
in the starting eleven today.

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:27.050
As the eldest son of the Zaizen family, 
you have to always be at the top.

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:30.790
If you don't make it back into the 
starting lineup by the next match,

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:33.790
you will give up soccer altogether.

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:37.170
This is bad!

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:40.650
I'm standing on the edge 
of the abyss. So please!

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:44.300
Teach me how to play soccer!

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:45.990
I'm begging you, Gotou!

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:46.660
Huh?

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:52.690
But... why me?

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:57.310
I mean, Coach is a judo nut. 
And our captain's like <i>that</i>...

00:11:57.310 --> 00:12:01.820
Our pivotal player, Aoyama, isn't really
 the type to teach anyone anything.

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:05.530
And learning from an underclassman is kinda...

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:07.330
<i>But I'm a first-year, too!</i>

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:10.950
That's why I thought of you and 
how you played at the training camp.

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:14.210
I will do anything to get better!

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:16.130
So please, Gotou!

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:20.450
S—

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.090
"S—"?

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:27.640
Starting lineup or not, it doesn't give 
your father grounds to make you quit.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:29.970
I don't know if I can help you,

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:35.350
but making the clubhouse and players 
shine is all part of the manager's job!

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:37.850
If I'm good enough, I will help.

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:41.990
Is Zaizen going to be okay?

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:46.620
Kaocchi's weakness is that he's absolutely
terrible at shooting with his feet.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:50.610
In order to get back among the starters,
 he has to stamp out that weakness.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.540
It'll all come down to Kaocchi's efforts.

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:57.890
It's so bright.

00:12:57.890 --> 00:13:03.150
Huh? There's so many more lights...

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:04.720
<b>Give it 
your best, 
Kaocchi!
- Dad</b>

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:09.220
E-Every single goal you've 
scored has been headed.

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:11.100
I'm confident in my heading ability.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:14.770
Turn that on its head, and it means 
every other part of your game is abysmal.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:18.360
If you focus on improving your strengths, 
you can wipe out your shortcomings!

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:21.430
That's what my dadd—my father says.

00:13:21.430 --> 00:13:24.360
You lost your starting spot!
They're clearly not wiped out!

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:31.870
First, let's start with ten shots from here
and get you up to a 50 percent hit rate.

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:35.440
Really? 50 percent?

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:36.410
Yes.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.510
You're a tough taskmaster, Gotou.

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:43.130
This is shockingly easy!

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:46.890
Ow!

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:47.630
Sorry!

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:51.650
Two goals from ten shots.

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:56.350
It makes sense that you can't score
with your feet in a match.

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:02.110
<i>His form isn't bad, so how 
can he be this terrible?</i>

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:05.330
Well, then...

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:07.900
Let's call it a day.

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:11.890
Wh-Wh-Why are you heading home already?!

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:17.450
The number of chances
you get in life are limited.

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:18.350
Huh?

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:20.920
In order to seize them...

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:26.400
If you don't practice with the mindset 
that it's the real deal, there's no point!

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:29.150
...is what my dadd—my father says.

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:31.180
<i>I-I see.</i>

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:32.050
See ya.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:34.560
No, no, no, no, no!

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:37.330
That mindset is what's holding you back!

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:39.810
Huh? I can try again?

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:42.310
Yo, do it already.
Until you get up to 50 percent!

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:45.070
Okay! Okay! Okay!

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:46.650
Jeeves.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:48.320
Yes, Master?

00:14:48.770 --> 00:14:50.880
Isn't Kaoru back yet?

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:54.950
I believe he's committed himself 
to a spot of secret training, sir.

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:57.330
Secret training?

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:58.140
There!

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:00.670
There!

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:04.210
It's no good. He's not getting any better!

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:06.630
Hey, Kaoru.

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:09.810
I've been watching for a while.

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:15.390
You've practiced until this hour, but your
 shots haven't improved in the slightest.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:23.610
However! There is no shortcut to success!

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:26.070
Dadd—Father.

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:27.360
Sir!

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:29.300
But on this occasion...

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:34.120
I <i>will</i> get you back in the starting eleven!

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:35.910
Where's the coach?

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:36.990
Daddy!

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:41.290
Daddy...

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:42.390
Kaocchi!

00:15:43.510 --> 00:15:45.500
You...

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:46.750
...absolute...

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:48.510
...idiots!

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:51.050
This is exactly why we're in this situation!

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:54.410
Ow.

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:56.730
I see now.

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:01.520
My methods were completely wrong.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:05.970
K-Kaocchi, who is she?

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:07.410
Gotou.

00:16:08.870 --> 00:16:09.680
Back to work.

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:11.280
Y-Yes, miss!

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:26.130
Again.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:32.590
Um, it's already past dinnertime, 
so could we maybe call it—

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:43.430
You got half in!

00:16:44.510 --> 00:16:45.940
You did it.

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:47.600
Daddy!

00:16:47.600 --> 00:16:48.630
Kaocchi!

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:49.840
Daddy!

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:51.420
Kaocchi!

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:54.100
Okay, not yet. Ten more reps.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:00.350
Sa-ka-i! Sa-ka-i!

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:02.390
Amazing Sakai!

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:06.790
He's on fire again.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.840
I can hear it today, too.

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:12.970
Yes! Amazing!

00:17:11.190 --> 00:17:11.840
All right!

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:14.660
How about this?

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:19.720
Huh? What's this?

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:22.390
<i>I can hear it! I can hear it!</i>

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:24.980
<i>The whisper telling me to go score!</i>

00:17:26.070 --> 00:17:28.630
<i>I'll show you the fruits of my training!</i>

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:33.030
Oh? You're not Aoyama?

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:33.740
Huh?

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:38.570
I made a mistake. Sorry. Sorry.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:40.810
Huh?

00:17:40.810 --> 00:17:41.630
What?!

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:47.470
It was all a misunderstanding?!

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:51.350
Y-Yeah, just how I planned it.

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:56.510
I can hear the whispers 
of the God of Soccer!

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:59.260
Sounds like those whispers keep on coming.

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:02.720
I can hear it!

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:03.120
I can hear!

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:06.950
Hm?

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:13.230
<i>What's going on? I can't 
hear the whispers anymore.</i>

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:15.790
Don't worry, Sakai!

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:20.420
If you can't score, just come back to us!

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:23.490
Hey, hey, come on! Hey, come on!

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:23.490
What?!

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:27.870
This is bad!

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:31.550
Hey, hey, come on! Hey, come on!

00:18:31.550 --> 00:18:35.150
S-S-Sakai, come back to us!

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:38.240
The village of rejects is fun.

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:38.880
Hey!

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:40.210
Dammit!

00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:43.510
I never want to go back there!

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:52.520
Huh? You changed your hair back?

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:56.380
Why don't you just come back, Sakai?

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:59.030
Hey, hey, come on! Hey, come on!

00:18:59.810 --> 00:19:05.030
<i>If I embrace being Aoyama, both physically 
and mentally, I should awaken again!</i>

00:19:05.030 --> 00:19:07.360
Sakai-senpai!

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:09.830
<i>I need to be cool towards my fans, too.</i>

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:11.790
He's just going to ignore them?

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.540
That's boring!

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:21.430
The awakened Sakai was fun, 
but a cool one is boring!

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:26.420
Could you please refrain from pantsing me?

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:27.700
What?!

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:29.930
No, seriously, pull his pants back up!

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:33.810
<i>I have to accelerate my Aoyama-fication.</i>

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:37.440
<b>Aoyama Life</b>

00:19:34.510 --> 00:19:36.930
Huh? I... what?

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:42.010
As you can see, I'm trying 
to become Aoyama right now.

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:46.220
Since you're nothing like him 
whatsoever, I didn't realize.

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:47.450
What?!

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:52.470
I imitated him and awoke as a goal poacher!

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:02.470
So if I can fully transform into
Aoyama, I can once again—

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:04.090
Shut up!

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:08.540
I'm begging you, Gotou-chan!

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:11.230
What do I need to do to get closer to Aoyama?

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:13.370
I want to go back one more time!

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:16.100
To that shining version of myself!

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:19.360
U-Um, Sakai-san...

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:24.550
The new victory dance!

00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:24.550
If you're joking, stop right now.

00:20:26.210 --> 00:20:31.250
Are you trying to defile Aoyama-kun?!

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:41.260
I can't hear it!

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:38.250
What are you doing, Sakai?

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:41.260
He's not on his game today, either.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:51.140
Yeah!

00:20:51.690 --> 00:20:53.140
Gotou!

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:55.370
Aoyama!

00:20:56.400 --> 00:21:00.970
<i>Please! Hear! Hear it!</i>

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:03.650
Gola, golazo!

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:04.900
<i>There!</i>

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:10.110
Vai! Gola, golazo!

00:21:10.110 --> 00:21:13.060
Gola, gola, golazo!

00:21:13.060 --> 00:21:16.070
Gola, gola, golazo!

00:21:16.070 --> 00:21:20.910
Vai! Go, go, go, golazo!

00:21:23.430 --> 00:21:26.370
What is he doing? Gross!

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:28.550
That's so lame!

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:33.510
Sakai has reverted to his stooge form,
so I guess Kaocchi will be our striker again.

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:34.630
Yes.

00:23:09.010 --> 00:23:10.460
Hey.

00:23:10.460 --> 00:23:13.290
What's the commotion? Did something happen?

00:23:13.290 --> 00:23:14.160
That.

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:19.170
Who are those men talking to Aoyama?

00:23:19.170 --> 00:23:21.540
People from the youth division.

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:23.360
Here to scout.

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:24.540
What?

00:23:26.230 --> 00:23:29.550
Aoyama might quit the team.

00:23:30.810 --> 00:23:32.300
What's <i>that </i>supposed to mean?!

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>The Reason Behind Aoyama-kun's Choice</b>
